response:
The report describes a cyberattack targeting Ukraine attributed with medium confidence to threat actor UAC-0057 (UNC1151 / Ghostwriter). The attack chain involves a nested RAR archive ("Диверсанти.rar" containing "Диверсанти 21.03.rar", which contains an SFX archive "Диверсанти filercs.rar" disguised using RTLO). The SFX archive contains decoy files and a VBScript file named "Thumbs.db", which creates and launches a .NET binary "dhdhk0k34.com". This ultimately leads to the deployment and infection with Cobalt Strike Beacon via an injector "inject.exe". Various indicators of compromise including file hashes, domains, and URLs are provided.

